{
  "name": "Chhatri",
  "_about": "A CHHATRI: the domed kiosk of Mughal and Rajput building -- a raised platform, a ring of columns, the deep eave (chhajja) they carry, a low drum and an onion on it, a finial. Written once and used wherever one stands: on the Taj Mahal's roof, on top of its minarets. `r` is the circle the columns stand on; everything else is in proportion to it unless given.",
